{
 "_meta": {
  "purpose": "Consensus sanity check on top of the statistical ratings (ratings follow-up, user-approved). Per position, the players a knowledgeable fan would accept in an all-time top 3, and two consensus OVR anchors. tools/ratings/consensus.ts compares the statistical top 3 with these lists and writes the 'Consensus check' section of docs/RATINGS_REPORT.md.",
  "rule": "The statistical ratings are primary and win every conflict. Nothing in this file changes a rating: the engine (src/engine/ratings) never reads it. When stats and consensus disagree, the stats result is kept and the disagreement is flagged in the report.",
  "tiers": {
   "all-time": "Default. The NFL 100th Anniversary All-Time Team (2019, 26-voter panel of coaches, executives, former players and media) at the player's position. The team was 'voted in no order' within each position group, so every member counts equally.",
   "modern": "Careers that matured after the 2019 vote cannot be on that team. Such a player is added only when he has a public, countable record that only All-Time Team members otherwise share at his position (a third Super Bowl MVP, a third AP Defensive Player of the Year). Kept deliberately short; everyone else outside the All-Time Team is a disagreement to flag, not a failure."
  },
  "positions": "Pool positions: QB, RB, WR, TE, DE, DT, LB, CB, S; the OL pool is split by slot (tackles LT/RT, guards LG/RG, center C) the way the All-Time Team splits OT/OG/C. The team's OLB and MLB groups are both LB. An offensive lineman on the team at another OL spot (e.g. Larry Allen, listed at guard, slotted at tackle in his unit) is accepted at any OL slot and the report says where he was listed.",
  "matching": "By name within the position (accents, punctuation and spaces folded, so 'Anthony Muñoz' = 'Anthony Munoz' and 'O. J. Simpson' = 'O.J. Simpson'), any stint. Players from before the 1960s (Baugh, Graham, Hutson, ...) are not in the legacy pool and never match.",
  "fetched": "Wikipedia pages read once each with action=raw (User-Agent BeatTheBeasts-DataBuilder/0.1), 2026-09-23, serially with pauses. NFL.com articles are cited as the Wikipedia article cites them; they were not fetched. Pro-Football-Reference was not used."
 },
